3	//! `ServiceAccountService`: service-account lifecycle use cases — create/get/list/archive
4	//! (SMA-445 Task 16). Mirrors `RoleService`'s DI + authorize pattern (`application/roles.rs:
5	//! 78-204`): every method authorizes BEFORE mutating/reading. The Cedar resource is always the
6	//! service account's OWNER tenancy node, never the service account's own principal PRN — the
7	//! embedded schema only lets `CreateServiceAccount`/`GetServiceAccount`/`ListServiceAccounts`/
8	//! `ArchiveServiceAccount` apply to `[Root, Organization, Team, Project]` (`authz/schema.rs`),
9	//! and `TenancyNodeRef` itself has no `Root` arm (a service account's owner is always a
10	//! concrete node, `ck_service_account_owner`), so [`owner_resource_prn`] only ever needs the
11	//! three node arms.
12	//!
13	//! `archive`'s cache-eviction step (spec §9/D5, "revocation-vs-cache honesty") is the
14	//! security-critical half of this file: once `set_principal_status` disables the SA, every one
15	//! of its cached positive API-key validations must stop authenticating immediately —
16	//! `AuthenticateApiKey` (Task 18) checks `ApiKeyValidationCache::get` before ever touching
17	//! Postgres, so a stale entry would let a disabled SA's key keep authenticating for up to the
18	//! cache's TTL. `keys`/`cache` are `Arc<dyn ...>` trait objects (not generic-DI) — the same
19	//! shared handles a later task's `AppState`/`ApiKeyService`/`AuthenticateApiKey` wiring will
20	//! reuse, mirroring `RoleService::grants`'s own `Arc<dyn RoleGrantStore>` rationale (module
21	//! docs there). `repo`/`ids`/`clock` stay generic-DI, mirroring `ProjectService`/`TeamService`.
22	//!
23	//! **`entity_gen` bump deferred (Task 16 brief, spec §6/D16).** Every OTHER write that bumps
24	//! `entity_gen` (org/team/project `set_status`, role grant/revoke, policy CRUD) does so INSIDE
25	//! its `Pg*` persistence adapter via a `gens: Generations` field threaded through the
26	//! adapter's own constructor (`PgOrganizationRepository::new(db, gens)`, etc.) — no
27	//! application service ever imports `crate::adapters::authz::Generations` directly (grepped:
28	//! zero such imports anywhere under `application/`). `PgServiceAccountRepository` (Task 9,
29	//! already implemented and covered by `tests/service_accounts.rs`) was built WITHOUT a `gens`
30	//! field, so bumping `entity_gen` from here would mean either (a) reaching into
31	//! `crate::adapters::authz::Generations` straight from the application layer — breaking the
32	//! hexagonal boundary every sibling service respects — or (b) reopening Task 9's already-
33	//! committed `PgServiceAccountRepository` constructor and its passing persistence-test suite —
34	//! both outside this task's declared file list (`src/application/service_accounts.rs` +
35	//! `application/mod.rs`). Deferred to whichever future task wires `ServiceAccountService` into
36	//! `AppState`, which can thread `gens` into `PgServiceAccountRepository::set_principal_status`
37	//! exactly like every sibling `Pg*Repository` does. Harmless today: (1) no current Cedar policy
38	//! reads `principal.status` (brief), and (2) a disabled SA is already blocked twice over
39	//! without it — this archive's own cache-evict step below, plus Task 18's authentication-time
40	//! `PrincipalStatus` check.
