3	//! Postgres-backed `PolicyStore` (SeaORM). `put` validates the Cedar source against the
4	//! embedded schema before touching the database, and — like `delete` — rejects any
5	//! mutation of an existing `system = true` row (`AuthzError::SystemImmutable`); a *new*
6	//! row with `system = true` (the seeding path, Task 17) is not rejected, only edits/deletes
7	//! of an already-persisted system row are. `list_all` reads every row in one REPEATABLE
